29648: *Note: This is a split field.
29649: 
29650: n  sh[5] || sh[0-4] r  ROTL[64](rS, n) b  mb[5] || mb[0-4] m  MASK(b, � n) rA  r & m
29651: The contents of rS are rotated left the number of bits specified by operand SH. A mask is generated having 1 bits from bit [MB] through bit [63 - SH] and 0 bits elsewhere. The rotated data is ANDed with the generated mask and the result is placed into rA.
29652: 
29653: This instruction is defined only for 64-bit implementations. Using it on a 32-bit implementation will cause the system illegal instruction error handler to be invoked.
29654: 
29655: Note that rldic can be used to clear and shift bit fields using the methods shown below:
29656: � To clear the high-order b bits of the contents of a register and then shift the result left by n bits, set SH = n and MB = b - n.
29657: � To clear the high-order n bits of a register, set SH = 0 and MB = n.
29658: 
29659: Other registers altered:
29660: � Condition Register (CR0 field): Affected: LT, GT, EQ, SO
29661: 
29662: (if Rc = 1)
29663: 
29664: Simplified mnemonics:
29665: 
29666: clrlsldi rA,rS,b,n
29667: 
29668: equivalent to
29669: 
29670: rldic rA,rS,n,b - n
29671: 
29672: For a more detailed list of simplified mnemonics for the rldic instruction, refer to Appendix E Simplified Mnemonics.
