29737: The contents of rS are rotated left the number of bits specified by operand SH. A mask is generated having 1 bits from bit MB through bit 63 and 0 bits elsewhere. The rotated data is ANDed with the generated mask and the result is placed into rA.
29738: 
29739: This instruction is defined only for 64-bit implementations. Using it on a 32-bit implementation will cause the system illegal instruction error handler to be invoked.
29740: 
29741: Note that rldicl can be used to extract, rotate, shift, and clear bit fields using the methods shown below:
29742: � To extract an n-bit field, that starts at bit position b in rS, right-justified into rA (clearing the remaining 64-n bits of rA), set SH = b + n and MB = 64 - n.
29743: � To rotate the contents of a register left by n bits, set SH = n and MB = 0; to rotate the contents of a register right by n bits, set SH = (64 - n), and MB = 0.
29744: � To shift the contents of a register right by n bits, set SH = 64 - n and MB = n.
29745: � To clear the high-order n bits of a register, set SH = 0 and MB = n.
29746: 
