29909: The contents of rS are rotated left the number of bits specified by operand SH. A mask is generated having 1 bits from bit MB through bit 63 - SH and 0 bits elsewhere. The rotated data is inserted into rA under control of the generated mask.
29910: 
29911: This instruction is defined only for 64-bit implementations. Using it on a 32-bit implementation will cause the system illegal instruction error handler to be invoked.
29912: 
29913: Note: rldimi can be used to insert an n-bit field, that is right-justified in rS, into rA starting at bit position b, by setting SH = 64 - (b + n) and MB = b.
