30181: sc
30182: System Call (x'4400 0002')
30183: 
30184: Programming Environments Manual PowerPC RISC Microprocessor Family
30185: sc
30186: 
30187: Reserved
30188: 
30189: 17
30190: 
30191: 00 000
30192: 
30193: 0 0000
30194: 
30195: 0
30196: 
30197: 56
30198: 
30199: 10 11
30200: 
30201: 15 16
30202: 
30203: 0000 0000 0000 00
30204: 
30205: 10 29 30 31
30206: 
30207: In the PowerPC UISA, the sc instruction calls the operating system to perform a service. When control is returned to the program that executed the system call, the content of the registers depends on the register conventions used by the program providing the system service.
30208: 
30209: This instruction is context synchronizing, as described in Section 4.1.5.1 Context Synchronizing Instructions.
30210: 
30211: Other registers altered: � Dependent on the system service
30212: 
30213: In PowerPC OEA, the sc instruction does the following: SRR0  iea CIA + 4 SRR1[33-36,42-47]  0 SRR1[0-32,37-41,48-63]  MSR[0-32,37-41,48-63] MSR  new_value (see below) NIA  0x0000 _0000_0000_0C00
30214: The EA of the instruction following the sc instruction is placed into SRR0. Bits [0-32, 37-41, 48-63] of the MSR are placed into the corresponding bits of SRR1, and bits [33-36 and 42-47] of SRR1 are set to zero.
30215: 
30216: Note: An implementation may define additional MSR bits, and in this case, may also cause them to be saved to SRR1 from MSR on an exception and restored to MSR from SRR1 on an rfid (or rfi).
30217: 
30218: Then a system call exception is generated. The exception causes the MSR to be altered as described in Section 6.4 Exception Definitions.
30219: 
30220: The exception causes the next instruction to be fetched from interrupt vector 0x00C00.
30221: 
30222: Note: sc serves as both a basic and an extended mnemonic. The Assembler recognizes an sc mnemonic with one operand as the basic form, and an sc mnemonic with no operand as the extended form.
30223: 
30224: Other registers altered:
30225: � SRR0 � SRR1 � MSR
