web search: https://powerpc.dev/general/PPC_Vers202_Book1_public.pdf
codex
The manual’s word-mask RTL raises another issue: wrapping masks may select the upper 32 bits, so truncation alone may leave Site B incomplete. I’m resolving that against the ISA text before judging its siblings. The gate premise also needs narrowing: the ASan sweep includes 64-bit PowerPC machine construction, while both dedicated PowerPC correctness gates use G4.

