codex
The ISA confirms the wraparound issue: `rlwinm` and `rlwnm` lose the upper half for wrapping masks, and `rlwimi` needs more than truncation in those cases. The existing witness’s oracle also mishandles wrapping masks, though its three quoted defect rows remain valid. I’m finishing detector rows that distinguish these failures from no-op and zero-result repairs.

